====================================================================
§4 Flag-type field diagnosis
====================================================================

- IsActive: **NO divergence in pre-consume window.** 0 warnings total.
- CurrentState: **NO divergence.** 0 warnings total.
- EventId, EventTick, StartTick, InheritEndTick, BlendEndTick,
  SuppressSteeringUntilTick, RoomBypassUntilTick: **all 0 warnings.**

Both sides agree that handoff is inactive for the entire pre-consume window
(IsActive=false, CurrentState=Normal, EventId=0, all tick fields=0). The
ONLY divergent field is SnapshotRotation, and only by exactly 180.000000 deg —
a fixed, value-independent constant. This is NOT a populated-vs-default
mismatch; both sides hold default(Quaternion) = (0,0,0,0).

Root cause is NOT in the _handoffState pre-populate path — no _handoffState
field ever disagrees. Root cause is in the SnapshotRotation comparator:

  float rotDelta = Quaternion.Angle(realHof.SnapshotRotation, shadowHof.SnapshotRotation);
  (BuddahPredictedMotor.cs:1599-1603)

Quaternion.Angle(default, default) returns exactly 180 deg because the Unity
formula is approximately 2*acos(clamp(|dot|,0,1)), and dot((0,0,0,0),(0,0,0,0))=0
=> 2*acos(0) = 180. Both sides store (0,0,0,0) (struct-default), so the values
are bit-identical; the comparator simply mis-scores bit-identical default quats
as "180 deg apart". Once a real handoff consume runs (T~=2790..2910), both sides
receive a real projected quaternion (not default) and Quaternion.Angle correctly
returns 0.

====================================================================
§5 VERDICT + hypothesis ranking
====================================================================

VERDICT: **Comparator false positive. No actual shadow divergence.**

Evidence: single-field divergence with exactly one observed angle-deg value
(180.000000, zero variance, zero dependence on tick / input / state), occurring
uniformly from the first comparison tick, and vanishing the instant a real
handoff consume fires on both sides. All 14 sibling fields (including the
IsActive/CurrentState flags that would gate a legitimate populate/default split)
are bit-identical. This is the canonical signature of the Quaternion.Angle
default-quaternion bug — NOT a state-capture-timing bug.

Hypothesis ranking:

1. (CONFIRMED) Quaternion.Angle default-vs-default false positive.
   Evidence:
   - Exactly 180.000000 deg, zero variance, 4550 samples.
   - All other 14 handoff fields exhibit 0 divergences — including IsActive,
     which would have to mismatch if the state-capture path differed between
     real and shadow.
   - Divergence vanishes at the first hof-consume (T~=2910 heartbeat) because
     both sides then hold real quaternions, not default ones.
   - motor.cs:373 assigns _realScratch.ShadowHandoffState = _handoffState (a
     default struct while inactive) and BuddahHandoffStep.cs:30-44 likewise
     returns state built from ctx.ShadowPreHandoffState (default) through
     Advance(...) which never writes SnapshotRotation. Both end up with
     default(Quaternion) = (0,0,0,0).

2. (REJECTED) Pre-populate path timing bug. Would require at least IsActive
   or one tick-field to also diverge — observed count is 0 on every such field.

3. (REJECTED) Transient-at-consume-only. Warnings are continuous across 2432
   ticks, not transient; they actually STOP at the consume.

Recommendation: **direct fix — no Step 3 outside-RunInputs audit needed.**

Proposed fix site (non-binding, no .cs change performed): in
BuddahPredictedMotor.cs around line 1599, guard Quaternion.Angle against
default quaternions. Options (pick one during implementation):
  a) Skip the comparison when both sides are default:
       if (realHof.SnapshotRotation != default && shadowHof.SnapshotRotation != default) { ... }
  b) Gate on IsActive (both sides agree it's false already):
       if (realHof.IsActive || shadowHof.IsActive) { ... Quaternion.Angle ... }
  c) Compare components directly with tolerance:
       Vector4 dq = new Vector4(r.x-s.x, r.y-s.y, r.z-s.z, r.w-s.w);
       if (dq.sqrMagnitude > 1e-8f) { ... }
Option (b) is cleanest and aligns with the semantic "SnapshotRotation is only
defined when handoff is active."

Confirmation: 74 FATAL emissions and 4550 warnings are noise from this one
comparator site. Once the guard lands, phase 3d parity audit will be clean
end-to-end (loc/imp/tel/mod/hof all equal).

